Local change (marked "amiga-pi"), so no floating point is compiled in: vbcc
keeps unused static functions, and a float operation on a 68020 without an
FPU calls mathieeesingbas.library, which amiga-pi does not open:
  stb_image.h        stbi_hdr_to_ldr_gamma/_scale under #ifndef STBI_NO_HDR
  stb_image_write.h  the JPEG writer under #ifndef STBIW_NO_JPEG
sha256 after it
  5c0dfbd20ea723c215da6ac09906e08f37aff290481ec43483799c4b72bd56c1  stb_image.h
  b9f8e7f4fe8fa6d2c3da21e1488f2a898bce8151adf89f1435164e8d44e9e874  stb_image_write.h

amiga-pi's read decodes PNG, JPEG, BMP and GIF with stb_image and writes
PNG with stb_image_write (amiga-pi/image.c, compiled through
amiga-pi/stb_impl.c), as pi's read shrinks images and turns BMP into PNG.
